<title>INDIA: Indian cotton markets shut for Hindu festival.</title>
<headline>Indian cotton markets shut for Hindu festival.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian cotton markets were closed on Thursday for a Hindu festival holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, Indian cotton prices held steady in a narrow price band. &quot;Demand from millers as well as yarn manufacturers remained low but thin supplies kept prices intact,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>The markets reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
